            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0629" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2359</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5586</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-29">October 29, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        30.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    5588 of October 28, 1937, and to enclose (1) a copy of a strictly informal
                    memorandum of points suggested for adjustment and (2) a translation of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">acuerdo</hi> which reached the representatives of the
                    landowners of the Yaqui Valley in Mexico City yesterday evening at about half
                    past nine.…</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I expect Licenciado Beteta to advise me today of the outcome of his conversation
                    with President Cárdenas last night. I believe that, as President Cardenas
                    apparently issued his <hi rendition="#italic">acuerdo</hi> before receiving the
                    views for which he had asked me and since the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >acuerdo</hi> was made public here in this morning’s newspapers, there is
                    little likelihood of obtaining the delay for harvesting the crop in June which
                    was requested. It is possible, however, that if we continue to press for other
                    points connected with the transfer of non-irrigated lands in exchange for
                    irrigated lands provided for in the <hi rendition="#italic">acuerdo</hi>, some
                    results helpful to the American landowners may yet be obtained.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>



